      "content": "Your partner is likely experiencing Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA), a life-threatening emergency where the body burns fat for fuel, producing toxic acids that cause nausea, confusion, and a fruity breath odor.\nThey absolutely need to drink water immediately, but you must also administer a rapid-acting insulin dose and check their blood glucose and ketone levels right now.\nIf they become unresponsive, have trouble breathing, or their blood sugar stays above 250 mg/dL despite insulin, call 911 immediately because this is not something that can be \"slept off.\"",
